  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Khyber Pakhtunkhwa Food Security Support Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will address climate vulnerabilities, food security and livelihoods of rural farm households in the most flood-damaged districts of the Khyber Pakhtunkhwa province. The proposed project will contribute to (i) increased agricultural productivity by providing flood-affected smallholding farmers with critical agriculture inputs and training in the safe and efficient use of those agricultural inputs; (ii) improved household nutrition through agricultural input support and training to female farmers; (iii) improved digitalization for farmers to better access extension services, markets, and climate and disaster information; and (iv) increased institutional preparedness for climate-induced disasters with interventions utilizing information and communication technology. The project will contribute to the government&amp;apos;s Resilient Recovery, Rehabilitation, and Reconstruction Framework strategy and investment priority. It will bolster the agriculture sector&amp;apos;s response to the impact of the 2022 floods in the province and will support flood-affected smallholder (and tenant) farmers. The project will improve the resilience, livelihoods, and food security situation of rural households. The support will cover 23% of the area under wheat cultivation, 32% of the area under rice cultivation, and 50% of the area of vegetable cultivation in the project districts.</narrative>
  </description>
